    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p8_b33",
      "text": "We measure the number of preference tokens required to\nreach target HH win-rates on identical hardware. Table 11\nshows that TUR-DPO is more token-efficient than DPO and\napproaches PPO at higher targets without incurring rollout\noverhead. We attribute these gains to uncertainty weighting,\nwhich suppresses noisy updates, and to shaped rewards\nthat provide additional gradient signal on hard pairs. We\nalso track GPU hours, peak memory usage, and throughput.\nTUR-DPO operates within a modest factor of DPO and\nrequires substantially less memory and time than PPO.\n",
      "bbox": [
